    "done_when": "packages/imas-alambic/src/imas_alambic/pulse_writer.py owns the temporary name beside pulse_path, a dot-prefixed name of the form .900001_0.RANDOM.partial.nc for pulse 900001 run 0, made by tempfile.mkstemp in the output directory, that can never match pulse_path, and one module-private engine-owned context manager (leading underscore, not added to __all__, so the public surface is unchanged) yields that temporary path, gives it mode 0644 before os.replace onto pulse_path, and unlinks it on any exception; write_pulse writes through it and the existing-file refusal is unchanged. In the new packages/imas-alambic/tests/test_run_file_write.py, against a synthetic flat bundle, a write whose third IDS raises leaves neither 900001_0.nc nor any temporary file in the output directory; a clean write leaves exactly 900001_0.nc with mode 0644 under umask 022; a second write without overwrite is still refused. Negative control: write_pulse writing straight to the final name, as at base, fails the partial-write test, logged once. pytest packages/imas-alambic/tests tests/data/test_pulse_writer.py adds no failures against base, judged by failure ids from one base run and one head run, each logged once. In a separate style(format) commit that changes nothing else, ruff format brings packages/imas-alambic/src/imas_alambic/eddb_remote.py and packages/imas-alambic/src/imas_alambic/transform_engine.py to format, with REMOTE_SCRIPT byte-identical in value before and after, shown by comparing the string at both revisions. uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests packages exits 0. All runs on the fleet allocation in place.",
